  "goodToKnow": "Der Kurfürst is a prince-elector of the Holy Roman Empire, one of the princes entitled to elect the king. The Golden Bull of 1356 fixed seven electors: three archbishops (Mainz, Cologne, Trier) and four secular princes. Kur- comes from küren (to choose), not die Kur (spa cure). Saxony's Kurfürst Augustus the Strong made Dresden splendid. Der Fürst means prince. Weak noun: den Kurfürsten. Plural: die Kurfürsten."
